<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21177] volatile create in .lustre/fid prunes all cached FID dentries under the directory's d_lock</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21177</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Tools that move files by FID (lfs migrate, lfs mirror extend/split, movers and policy engines through llapi_create_volatile_idx(), the HSM copytool restore) create their volatile files in &amp;lt;mnt&amp;gt;/.lustre/fid. When the file goes to MDT0, every create cancels the client's UPDATE lock on .lustre/fid, and the cancel runs ll_prune_negative_children(), which walks one cached dentry per FID ever looked up under the d_lock of .lustre/fid. All FID path walks on the client spin on that lock meanwhile.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The cancel is not needed: a volatile file gets no name in the parent, and since &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14693" title="bypass DLM locking on parent directory for volatile files" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14693"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-14693&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (2.14.52) the MDT takes no lock on the parent for it. It happens twice per create:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;mdc_intent_open_pack() cancels the parent's UPDATE lock by ELC for every create, volatile or not.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;liblustreapi's create_volatile() and create_restore_volatile() unlink() the volatile name afterwards (for non-Lustre file systems). On Lustre that is an RPC failing with -ENOENT, and mdc_unlink() cancels the same lock first.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;One el9.8 client, master servers, 400k cached FIDs in .lustre/fid, volatile file on MDT0:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class='table-wrap'&gt;
&lt;table class='confluenceTable'&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th class='confluenceTh'&gt;client&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class='confluenceTh'&gt;master&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class='confluenceTh'&gt;mdc patch&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class='confluenceTh'&gt;mdc + llapi patches&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;llapi_create_volatile_idx() in .lustre/fid&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;90/s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;156/s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;1220/s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;prunes per create, each&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;2, 4.4 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;1, 4.8 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;raw volatile open() as lfs does it&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;174/s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;1234/s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;1227/s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;6 threads stat-ing FIDs beside llapi creates (84,000/s alone)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;3,134/s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;7,812/s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;78,319/s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Fix, two patches: no parent ELC in mdc_intent_open_pack() for MDS_CREATE_VOLATILE (an older MDT revokes the lock by blocking callback instead), and no unlink() in liblustreapi when the volatile open succeeded on Lustre, with sanity test_185b.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
